.el .ds Aq '
.TH snip-theme-import 1  "snip 0.5.3" 
.SH NAME
snip\-theme\-import \- Convert a base16 scheme file into a user theme
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsnip theme import\fR [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-library\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-syntax\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPATH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Convert a base16 scheme file into a user theme
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<AS>\fR
Name to save it under. Defaults to the file stem
.TP
\fB\-\-library\fR \fI<LIBRARY>\fR
Library root. Falls back to SNIP_LIBRARY, ancestor discovery, then config
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Structured output mode for commands that return records
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-syntax\fR \fI<SYNTAX>\fR
Use an embedded syntax theme instead of deriving one from the palette
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR
Color policy for terminal preview
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite an existing theme file
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Convert and print the theme without writing anything
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
Path to a base16 or base24 scheme file, or "\-" to read stdin
